# DOSE — developer SSH PUBLIC keys for the Raspberry Pi `claudeagent` account.
#
# ONLY public keys go here. A public key is safe to commit and share; it
# grants nothing on its own. NEVER put a private key in this file.
#
# The Pi bootstrap (tools/bootstrap_claude_access.py) installs every valid
# public key below into claudeagent's ~/.ssh/authorized_keys on the next
# update. Lines starting with '#' are ignored, and each key is verified by
# decoding its OpenSSH wire format — a placeholder or truncated line is
# rejected rather than written as a broken authorized_keys entry.
#
# To add another Mac, on THAT Mac run:
#     ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -f ~/.ssh/dose_pi_claude_ed25519 -C "dose-pi claude dev"
#     cat ~/.ssh/dose_pi_claude_ed25519.pub
# and paste the resulting single line below. The private key stays on the Mac.
#
# --- public key line(s) below this line ---

